node_modules
.env

# ==============================================================================
# GITIGNORE CONFIGURATION FILE (.gitignore)
# ==============================================================================
# This file tells Git which files, folders, or sensitive data to IGNORE.
# Anything listed here will not be tracked, committed, or pushed to GitHub.
# ==============================================================================

# 1. DEPENDENCY FOLDER
# Ignores the 'node_modules' directory.
# - Why: Contains thousands of external npm packages installed locally.
# - Reason: Extremely large in file size; can easily be re-installed using 'npm install'.
#node_modules

# 2. ENVIRONMENT & SECRETS FILE
# Ignores the '.env' file.
# - Why: Stores secret environment variables (e.g., MONGO_URI database password, API keys).
# - Reason: Keeps sensitive credentials private and prevents them from leaking on GitHub.
#.env